From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:29:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] abd: keep allocations for the ARC mapping out of the
 shrinker's wait

__folio_split() allocates xarray nodes with the gfp mask of the mapping
once release_folio has let a chunk of order 6 or more go, while the
migration batch it runs in still holds its other folios. A new inode gets
GFP_HIGHUSER_MOVABLE, and under __GFP_FS direct reclaim makes
arc_shrinker_scan() wait for eviction, with those folios locked.

Drop __GFP_FS from the mask of the mapping. Joining a buffer already
allocates with GFP_NOIO, and nothing else allocates for this inode.
---
 module/os/linux/zfs/abd_os.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/os/linux/zfs/abd_os.c b/module/os/linux/zfs/abd_os.c
index 7397006..711c7bc 100644
--- a/module/os/linux/zfs/abd_os.c
+++ b/module/os/linux/zfs/abd_os.c
@@ -1157,6 +1157,12 @@ abd_lru_init(void)
 	/* Indices are never reused, so a shadow of what left would only pile up. */
 	mapping_set_exiting(inode->i_mapping);
 	set_bit(AS_KERNEL_FILE, &inode->i_mapping->flags);
+	/*
+	 * A split allocates for the mapping while the migration batch it runs
+	 * in holds other folios: not with a mask the ARC shrinker waits under.
+	 */
+	mapping_set_gfp_mask(inode->i_mapping,
+	    mapping_gfp_mask(inode->i_mapping) & ~__GFP_FS);
 	atomic64_set(&abd_lru_next_index, 0);
 	abd_lru_inode = inode;
 	abd_lru_mapping = inode->i_mapping;
